<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sasanian conquest of Jerusalem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/614">614 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-sasanian-war-of-602-628">Byzantine–Sasanian War of 602–628</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sasanian conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> took place in 614 CE, when the city fell to the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> under his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz">Shahrbaraz</a> during the last great war between the Sasanian and Byzantine empires. The relic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/true-cross">True Cross</a> was carried off to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> cite the capture as a high point of Sasanian siege capability, though the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> later recovered the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sasanian-conquest-of-jerusalem.jpg" alt="Sasanian conquest of Jerusalem" width="320" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Getoryk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Byzantine_and_Sassanid_Empires_in_600_CE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
